 - Outputs/reference files should be JSON arrays. Each element may be a string or object containing `text`/`output` fields.
 - Future work: support tabular CSV, scored datasets, multi-turn conversations.
 
+## Threshold Support
+- CLI: `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option (repeatable) gates CI pipelines on metric scores.
+  - Example: `frai eval --outputs out.json --threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95`
+  - Exits 0 if all thresholds pass, 1 if any fail, 2 for usage errors (unknown metric, malformed format, out-of-range score).
+  - Always writes the report; `passed` field and `thresholds` list record outcome in JSON; Markdown gains "Thresholds" section.
+  - A metric without a score (e.g., exact_match with no references) fails its threshold.
+- Core: `generateReport` accepts optional `thresholds: { exact_match: 0.9 }` object; custom metrics work the same way.
+
 ## Extensibility Hooks
 - `frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` exposes `DEFAULT_METRICS`; additional metrics can be registered by passing custom evaluators to `runEvaluations`.
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
